# Web Design Anchor — Git attributes

# GAL execution state must stay byte-identical across checkouts.
#
# The test-first transition producer (`gal test-first-transition install`) does a
# raw SHA-256 compare-and-swap against the prompt bytes on disk, and the CAS
# journal records that same digest. With `core.autocrlf=true` and no attribute
# pinning, a checkout rewrites these files to CRLF, the on-disk digest stops
# matching the journal, and every later transition fails closed with
# `stale transition CAS`. The transition journal itself also rejects any record
# line containing a CR.
#
# Mirrors the same two lines in the GAL source repo's own .gitattributes.
.dev/plans/*.md         eol=lf
.dev/plans/*.prompt.md  eol=lf
docs/**/*.md            eol=lf
